From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:08:06 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 36/40] Plutonium: agents get the helper's tab tools on T3's
 tabs

T3's MCP server offered only the helper's window tools, so its agents had no
find, permissions, file pickers, printing or downloads in their tabs. Now it
also offers tab_requests (what a tab waits on: pending.permission, print,
fileChooser, and what it was refused or uses), find_in_tab,
answer_permission, request_permission, choose_files, print_tab,
cancel_print, list_printers, list_downloads and download_action.

They take T3's tabId, as preview tools do, and default to the tab preview
tools act on without one. The server finds the browser's id for it
(ServerBrowser.plutoniumTabId, from Plutonium.getTabs on the tab's own
connection) and the helper runs its tool on that tab for the thread.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
